<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §2. `forceRockTypes` is a genuine vanilla
  BiomeDef field (RimWorld/BiomeDef.cs:139, `public List<ThingDef>
  forceRockTypes`) read by World.NaturalRockTypesIn (RimWorld/Planet/
  World.cs:395-398, `tile.Tile.PrimaryBiome.forceRockTypes`) and by
  GenStep_RockChunks (RimWorld/GenStep_RockChunks.cs:48-49) — both
  confirmed via rimsage source read, not guessed. It is exactly the field
  the donor Alpha Biomes def used for AB_MechanoidIntrusion
  (vendor/mod_sources/AlphaBiomes_src/1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/
  Biomes_MechanoidIntrusion.xml:97, `<forceRockTypes><li>GU_AncientMetals</li>
  </forceRockTypes>`) before RUT_RustCathedral.xml replaced that biome def
  wholesale and dropped the field along with the (inactive-dependency)
  donor rock type.

  Restoring it here, pointed at this mod's own two wall tiers, so any
  vanilla system that asks "what is this map's natural rock" on a Cathedral
  map answers with Cathedral walls instead of default granite/sandstone —
  belt-and-suspenders alongside the dedicated, denser scatter step in
  RUT_CathedralWallScatter.xml, which is the mod's actual guarantee of wall
  coverage on this 211/236-flat-tile biome (forceRockTypes' own placement
  density on a mostly non-hilly biome is not proven independently sufficient
  by itself, hence not relied on alone).

  Patches UtinniPatches' own RUT_RustCathedral (mandrake.rut.patches) — a
  cross-mod patch rather than editing that file directly, so this mod stays
  self-contained and removable; loadAfter mandrake.rut.patches in About.xml
  guarantees the def already exists when this runs.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_RustCathedral"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_RustCathedral"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <forceRockTypes>
          <li>RUT_CathedralDeckPlate</li>
          <li>RUT_MineableDeadSmartsteel</li>
        </forceRockTypes>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
